(* Positional command-line arguments — ARO-0047 §Positional Arguments
 *
 * Run with: aro run ./Examples/PositionalArguments https://example.com 3
 *
 * The `takes` clause on Application-Start declares the positionals, in order.
 * They are then read exactly like flags, so `--url https://example.com` keeps
 * working for a caller who prefers it.
 *)

(Application-Start: Crawler takes <url> <depth>) {
    Extract the <site> from the <parameter: url>.
    Extract the <levels> from the <parameter: depth>.

    Log "site: ${<site>}" to the <console>.
    Log "depth: ${<levels>}" to the <console>.

    (* Every positional, in order — what a variadic tool reads instead. *)
    Extract the <args> from the <parameter: arguments>.
    Compute the <argument-count: length> from <args>.
    Log "arguments: ${<argument-count>}" to the <console>.

    Return an <OK: status> for the <startup>.
}
